WEBVTT

00:00:05.809 --> 00:00:09.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Tuesday the third. Can you all hear me?</v>

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.570
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, but someone's coming through twice.</v>

00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:18.539
<v David Whitfield>That'll be me. Laptop and headset both having a go.</v>

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.579
<v Priya Raman>One of you's quite enough, thanks.</v>

00:00:22.929 --> 00:00:24.679
<v David Whitfield>There. Constructive feedback as ever.</v>

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Everyone in?</v>

00:00:28.089 --> 00:00:32.289
<v Marcus Hale>I'm here, just not on camera. Teams has picked the ceiling again.</v>

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.049
<v Hannah Price>Very clean ceiling, to be fair.</v>

00:00:35.659 --> 00:00:41.259
<v David Whitfield>Before we start properly, that charity bake sale on Friday — apparently bought cakes are cheating.</v>

00:00:41.939 --> 00:00:44.390
<v Tomasz Nowak>Only if you leave the sticker on.</v>

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:47.579
<v Priya Raman>That's your entire quality process, is it?</v>

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:54.119
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a cake audit. Jamie Brennan and Callum Reid aren't with us today.</v>

00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:01.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie asked me to pass on that he's about halfway through recalibrating the sensors on the PRV on the boiler.</v>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:03.649
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, cheers.</v>

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:12.189
<v Sarah Okafor>And Cal's near miss write-up at the palletiser needs to come across to you, Haley. Can you take that over from him?</v>

00:01:14.569 --> 00:01:17.370
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll take that write-up over from Cal.</v>

00:01:18.239 --> 00:01:20.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. Pricey, how have yours gone?</v>

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:29.890
<v Hannah Price>Um, the jam and sensor checks — I've got the first half done. Jam's cleared; I haven't got through the sensor checks yet.</v>

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.489
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, thanks.</v>

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:37.140
<v Hannah Price>And my inspection for leaks is all done, all signed off.</v>

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:40.700
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nice one.</v>

00:01:42.319 --> 00:01:48.969
<v Priya Raman>While we're on finished bits, I finished the repair on the GT2 Number 2 Bearing last night. That's sorted.</v>

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.200
<v David Whitfield>Ah, lovely. Bet you were pleased to see the back of that.</v>

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.650
<v Priya Raman>Yeah. Not my favourite evening, put it that way.</v>

00:02:00.569 --> 00:02:08.969
<v Hannah Price>Only other thing from me, I noticed the big board was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down. Just an observation.</v>

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:11.159
<v Marcus Hale>Was that early on?</v>

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.729
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, early part of the shift. Nothing ongoing there.</v>

00:02:16.139 --> 00:02:18.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Two new bits this morning.</v>

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:29.080
<v Sarah Okafor>Haley, if you've got a spare minute, can you do a site visit at Kestrel Hydraulics Leeds with the contractor by end of day?</v>

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.719
<v Marcus Hale>I can't take that, sorry. Can't get away from the plant today.</v>

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:40.400
<v Sarah Okafor>No, fair enough. I wasn't sure whether you could get out.</v>

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:44.150
<v Marcus Hale>Could you take that one, boss?</v>

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:53.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll do the site visit at Kestrel Hydraulics Leeds with the contractor by end of day, if I've got a spare minute.</v>

00:02:54.539 --> 00:02:56.639
<v David Whitfield>A spare minute. Those mythical things.</v>

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.400
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. It's not a drop-everything one.</v>

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.699
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, you clipped there — drop everything?</v>

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Not a drop-everything one. Definitely a 'not' in there.</v>

00:03:08.159 --> 00:03:12.710
<v Sarah Okafor>Pricey, can you write up the near miss at the wrapper for Monday?</v>

00:03:14.879 --> 00:03:19.080
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll write up the near miss at the wrapper for Monday.</v>

00:03:21.009 --> 00:03:23.810
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, I spoke over the end of that.</v>

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.210
<v Hannah Price>You're all right, I'd finished.</v>

00:03:27.199 --> 00:03:32.449
<v David Whitfield>Just checking I hadn't drowned you out again. This headset's either nothing or full tannoy.</v>

00:03:33.449 --> 00:03:34.849
<v Priya Raman>Full tannoy's about right.</v>

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.849
<v Sarah Okafor>We heard you both. Thanks, Pricey.</v>

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:41.449
<v Hannah Price>No worries.</v>

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:44.259
<v Sarah Okafor>That's everything I've got. Anything we've missed?</v>

00:03:45.229 --> 00:03:46.629
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nothing else from me.</v>

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.240
<v Marcus Hale>No, all good here.</v>

00:03:51.639 --> 00:03:54.789
<v David Whitfield>Only that I'm feeling personally attacked over the cakes.</v>

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:59.669
<v Hannah Price>Nobody actually said you were buying them. Interesting confession, though.</v>

00:04:00.159 --> 00:04:01.560
<v David Whitfield>Right, I'm saying nothing.</v>

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Probably safest. Cheers, everyone.</v>
